@startuml
title SplitSmart - expense approval and pairwise payment sequence
actor Submitter
actor Reviewer
participant "Swing / future client" as Client
participant "Application Use Case" as App
participant "Domain Policies" as Domain
database "Repository / DB" as DB
participant "Notification Port" as Notify

Submitter -> Client : enter expense and participants
Client -> App : submitExpense(command, actor)
App -> Domain : validate amount, membership, payer, split
Domain --> App : exact BigDecimal shares or errors
alt invalid
  App --> Client : correction errors; no saved review
else valid
  App -> DB : transaction: pending expense + shares + inbox notices
  DB --> App : committed pending expense
  App -> Notify : dispatch/record notices to other members
  App --> Client : pending confirmation
end

Reviewer -> Client : approve or reject
Client -> App : decide(expenseId, decision, expectedVersion)
App -> Domain : authorize and transition
alt rejected
  App -> DB : transaction: decision + rejected state
  note right of DB
    No obligation entries;
    no balance effect.
  end note
else approved, another stage remains
  App -> DB : transaction: decision + next pending stage
else final approval
  App -> DB : transaction: decision + approved state + pair obligations
  note right of DB
    Unique source and version check
    prevent duplicate/racing posting.
  end note
end
DB --> App : committed result or conflict
App --> Client : current workflow state

Submitter -> Client : record payment to named payee
Client -> App : recordPayment(pair, amount, idempotencyKey)
App -> Domain : validate positive amount and named pair
App -> DB : transaction: check outstanding + post payment + update projection
note right of DB
  Proposed MVP rejects overpayment.
  Only the named pair changes.
  Semantic duplicate policy remains open.
end note
DB --> App : committed result or conflict
App --> Client : updated pairwise amount
@enduml
